artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $H : T^*M \to \mathbb{R}$ be a smooth (i.e. $C^\infty$) Tonelli Hamiltonian on the cotangent bundle of a closed connected manifold $M$, and let $f_H^t$ denote its Hamiltonian flow. Consider the energy level $H^{-1}(1)$. Recall:
\begin{itemize}
\item An invariant Borel probability measure $\mu$ for $f_H^t$ is called an ergodic minimal measure if it is ergodic and minimizes the action $\int L\,d\mu$ among invariant probability measures (where $L$ is the Lagrangian dual to $H$), with rotation vector taken into account in the usual Mather variational sense.
\item A locally minimizing orbit is one whose every compact piece minimizes the action among curves with the same endpoints lying in a fixed neighborhood (in the sense of Mañé/Mather).
\item An orbit is asymptotic to the set of locally minimizing orbits if its $\alpha$- and $\omega$-limit sets are contained in the closure of the union of supports of locally minimizing orbits.
\end{itemize}
Question: Is it true that for a $C^\infty$-generic Tonelli Hamiltonian $H$, there exists a closed connected subset $F \subset H^{-1}(1)$ that is invariant under $f_H^t$ and satisfies all three of the following conditions simultaneously?
\begin{enumerate}
\item $F$ contains the supports of all ergodic minimal measures of $H$ on the energy level $H^{-1}(1)$;
\item the orbits asymptotic to the locally minimizing orbits are dense in $F$;
\item the restricted flow $f_H^t|_F$ admits a dense orbit in $F$.
\end{enumerate}

